        -: 1712: */
        -: 1713:
        -: 1714:/* This flag is obsolete as recursive validation is now the default (and only
        -: 1715: * possible) behaviour. Simply don't use it any more in the new code. */
        -: 1716:#define wxWS_EX_VALIDATE_RECURSIVELY    0x00000000 /* used to be 1 */
        -: 1717:
        -: 1718:/*  wxCommandEvents and the objects of the derived classes are forwarded to the */
        -: 1719:/*  parent window and so on recursively by default. Using this flag for the */
        -: 1720:/*  given window allows to block this propagation at this window, i.e. prevent */
        -: 1721:/*  the events from being propagated further upwards. The dialogs have this */
        -: 1722:/*  flag on by default. */
        -: 1723:#define wxWS_EX_BLOCK_EVENTS            0x00000002
        -: 1724:
        -: 1725:/*  don't use this window as an implicit parent for the other windows: this must */
        -: 1726:/*  be used with transient windows as otherwise there is the risk of creating a */
        -: 1727:/*  dialog/frame with this window as a parent which would lead to a crash if the */
        -: 1728:/*  parent is destroyed before the child */
        -: 1729:#define wxWS_EX_TRANSIENT               0x00000004
